{"name":"Integrity","hex":"#233e57","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"integrity","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Steadfast adherence to a strict moral or ethical code.","The state of being wholesome; unimpaired"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/integrity"}],"entries":[{"title":"Integrity","blocks":[{"text":"Integrity is the quality of being honest and having a consistent and uncompromising adherence to strong moral and ethical principles and values.\nIn ethics, integrity is regarded as the honesty and truthfulness or earnestness of one's actions. Integrity can stand in opposition to hypocrisy. It regards internal consistency as a virtue, and suggests that people who hold apparently conflicting values should account for the discrepancy or alter those values."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Integrity","wikidata":"Q1329012"},{"title":"Integrity (band)","blocks":[{"text":"Integrity is an American hardcore punk band formed in Cleveland, Ohio in 1988, but based in Belgium since 2003. A pioneer of the metalcore genre, the band's merger of influences from hardcore punk and heavy metal music, as well as gothic rock, industrial, noise, doomsday cults and western esotericism, was widely influential on the subsequent development of hardcore and metal. The band was a defining part of the 1990s hardcore scene, influencing similarly influential bands such as Converge, Hatebreed and Killswitch Engage."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/Integrity_Tokyo_2017_unholy.jpg/330px-Integrity_Tokyo_2017_unholy.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Integrity_(band)","wikidata":"Q944143"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/Integrity_live_2.JPG/500px-Integrity_live_2.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commo